# Diagnostics that do not yet carry what a reader needs, one per line:
# <case> R13-0[b]#NN P0|P1|P2 <what is missing>
#
# Same contract as tests/c99.knownfail and the difftest lists: a listed case
# may fail, and a listed case that starts PASSING is a failure -- closing a
# gap means deleting its line.
#
# Opened 2026-09-30 by the R13-0/R13-0b diagnostic review (plan node N8).
# Measured per driver on df8cc9b4; the three drivers do not agree, and none of
# them gives both a position and the construct/header name:
#
#   07  only the PRODUCT lacks it; ua_ref already reports
#       `f.c:5:11: error: no such file for #include`.  So 07 is NOT listed here
#       (listing a case that passes on this route is a failure by the contract)
#       -- it is in tests/difftest.com.knownfail, which covers the product.
#   11  product  `reject: not covered: malformed preprocessing locations`   no position
#   29  product  `reject: not covered: function-like macro invocation`      no position
#   31  product  `unisacc: error: undefined function 'f'`                   no position
#       py_ref   `CError: line 853: ...` for a 13-line file    a position in
#                the spliced buffer passed off as the user's -- a wrong line
#                is worse than no line
fb12-11-comment-then-continuation R13-0b#11 P1 `reject: not covered:` carries no file:line:col
fb12-29-macro-more-than-8-params R13-0b#29 P1 `reject: not covered:` carries no file:line:col
fb12-31-unused-static-refs-undefined R13-0b#31 P1 `undefined function` carries no position (the call site is what a reader needs)
